# Byte-compared and line-parsed artifacts must check out byte-identical
# on every platform. Windows runners (and Windows contributors) default
# to core.autocrlf=true, whose LF->CRLF checkout rewrite broke the
# corvid-ffi header drift gate on the Windows CI leg (cbindgen renders
# LF; the committed copy came back CRLF) and would corrupt the golden
# fixtures' line protocol for smoke.c's tokenizer (a trailing CR rides
# the last token of every line).
crates/corvid-ffi/corvid.h text eol=lf
crates/corvid-ffi/golden/** text eol=lf
crates/corvid-ffi/c/** text eol=lf
docs/FFI.md text eol=lf
